Id:287444246\n54 1 Exploring Creator-Centric Methods for LLM-Assisted Interactive Storytelling https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287443401\n55 1 EvoSpark: Endogenous Interactive Agent Societies for Unified Long-Horizon Narrative Evolution https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287470582\n56 1 TaleFrame: An Interactive Story Generation System with Fine-Grained Control and Large Language Models https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:283457802\n57 1 CHAE: Fine-Grained Controllable Story Generation with Characters, Actions and Emotions https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/adaef97d036b82dbbe6582097b58711140577675\n58 1 Oak Story: Improving Learner Outcomes with LLM-Mediated Interactive Narratives https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:281664166\n59 1 Improving Pacing in Long-Form Story Planning https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1ac61e3da6dbb844537c0e94ff3b07561bcd21d4\n60 1 AlphaContext: An Evolutionary Tree-based Psychometric Context Generator for Creativity Assessment https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287635031\n61 1 BOOKAGENT: Orchestrating Safety-Aware Visual Narratives via Multi-Agent Cognitive Calibration https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287618206\n62 1 The Garden of Forking Paths: Narrative Arc-Conditioned Gameplay Planning https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287445551\n63 1 High-quality generation of dynamic game content via small language models: A proof of concept https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:285240942\n64 1 ConWriter: Transition-Constrained Stateful Long-Form Story Generation with Lightweight Neuro-Symbolic Consistency Control https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:290852632\n65 1 GraphStory: Collaborative Story Writing through Event-Based Narrative Editing https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:289300871\n66 1 PlotTwist: A Creative Plot Generation Framework with Small Language Models https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:286583895\n67 1 StoryState: Agent-Based State Control for Consistent and Editable Storybooks https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:285270576\n68 1 Aether Weaver: Multimodal Affective Narrative Co-Generation with Dynamic Scene Graphs https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280337281\n69 1 CreAgentive: An Agent Workflow Driven Multi-Category Creative Generation Engine https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:281682841\n70 1 WHAT-IF: Exploring Branching Narratives by Meta-Prompting Large Language Models https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:274777160\n71 1 Emerging Practices in LLM-integrated Game Writing https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:284312057\n72 1 LLM-Based Authoring of Agent-Based Narratives through Scene Descriptions https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:284133224\n73 1 TattleTale: Storytelling with Planning and Large Language Models https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/4957e0a29298aac65b7bbf6aa344c40d14bf1bca\n74 1 Harnessing Large Language Models for Scalable and Effective Formative Assessment in Higher Education: A Review https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:282358472\n75 1 SWAG: Storytelling With Action Guidance https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:267499853\n76 1 The Bias that Lies Beneath: Qualitative Uncovering of Stereotypes in Large Language Models https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:270525555\n77 1 MUSE: A Multi-agent Framework for Unconstrained Story Envisioning via Closed-Loop Cognitive Orchestration https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:285275953\n78 1 Latent Planning Emerges with Scale https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287436207\n79 1 Camera Artist: A Multi-Agent Framework for Cinematic Language Storytelling Video Generation https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287351551\n80 1 HAWK: A Hierarchical Workflow Framework for Multi-Agent Collaboration https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280136679\n81 1 CineVerse: Consistent Keyframe Synthesis for Cinematic Scene Composition https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:278165423\n82 1 VisAgent: Narrative-Preserving Story Visualization Framework https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:276775681\n83 1 From Personas to Plot: Character-Grounded Multi-Agent Story Generation for Long-Form Narratives https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:289706462\n84 1 RPGAgent: Driving Coherent Story-to-Play Generation with an LLM-Based Multi-Agent System https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287442220\n85 1 CineAGI: Character-Consistent Movie Creation through LLM-Orchestrated Multi-Modal Generation and Cross-Scene Integration https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287782548\n86 1 PlayWrite: A Multimodal System for AI Supported Narrative Co-Authoring Through Play in XR https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:286228871\n87 1 From Extraction to Synthesis: Entangled Heuristics for Agent-Augmented Strategic Reasoning https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280053711\n88 1 Looking beyond the next token https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:277786921\n89 1 Story3D-Agent: Exploring 3D Storytelling Visualization with Large Language Models https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:271915816\n90 1 From Text-First to Structure-First: A Visual Pipeline for Narrative Writing https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287442948\n91 1 CUNI at SemEval-2026 Task 4: Multi-Head Narrative Aspect Disentanglement via Entangled Synthetic Dataset https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:289773832\n92 1 Semantic Prompting: Agentic Incremental Narrative Refinement through Spatial Semantic Interaction https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287669147\n93 1 Sparse Activation Editing for Reliable Instruction Following in Narratives https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:278789463\n94 1 RH-RAG: Trustworthy Long-Form Generation for Privacy-Constrained Settings https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:290831504\n95 1 Robo-Blocks: Generative Scaffolding in End-User Design and Programming of Social Robots https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:288702101\n96 1 StoryCrafter: A Graph-Based Co-Creative AI System Supporting Parental Story Re-Authoring https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287441629\n97 1 PICTURE: Enhancing Theory-of-Mind in Large Language Models by Revealing, Not Hiding, Characters' Lack of Knowledge https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:289813205\n98 1 CamPilot: A Multi-Agent Cinematic Assistant for Camera-Controlled Movie Generation https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:291901758\n99 1 Diving into Co-Creativity: Interaction Depth and Sentence Framing as Design Levers for Co-writing with AI https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:287441207\n100 1 Steering Emotional Dynamics for Art Therapy: Controllable Narrative Script Generation through Hierarchically Guided LLM Agents https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:289299712\n101 1 GENIE: A Fine-Grained Measure for Novelty https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:289187243\n102 1 MultiVerse: A Creator-Centered Approach to Steering Context-Adaptive Lyrics https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:291252505\n103 1 Chain-of-MetaWriting: Linguistic and Textual Analysis of How Small Language Models Write Young Students Texts https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:274859323\n104 1 Trailer Reimagined: An Innovative, Llm-DRiven, Expressive Automated Movie Summary framework (TRAILDREAMS) https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280358435\n105 1 ParaScopes: What do Language Models Activations Encode About Future Text? https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:282740206\n106 1 EvolvR: Self-Evolving Pairwise Reasoning for Story Evaluation to Enhance Generation https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280561069\n107 1 Narrative Context Protocol: An Open-Source Storytelling Framework for Generative AI https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280337410\n108 1 ViStoryBench: Comprehensive Benchmark Suite for Story Visualization https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:286976108\n109 1 Multiverse of Greatness: Generating Story Branches with LLMs https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:274192581\n110 1 Multigenre AI-powered Story Composition https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:269757073\n111 1 Generating Narrative Text in a Switching Dynamical System https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:215415939\n112 1 Narrative Text Generation with a Latent Discrete Plan https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:222178963\n113 1 Multimodal acting in mixed reality interactive storytelling https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:11783914\n114 1 From computer games to interactive stories: interactive storytelling https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:206374560\n115 1 Tricking LLM-Based NPCs into Spilling Secrets https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:280918656\n116 1 Affective and Dynamic Beam Search for Story Generation https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:264436541\n117 1 Chain-of-Lure: A Universal Jailbreak Attack Framework using Unconstrained Synthetic Narratives https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:282991947\n118 1 Agentic-ToM: Cognition-Inspired Agentic Processing For Enhancing Theory of Mind Reasoning https://api.semanticscholar.org/CorpusId:282900318\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> notes/reading_log.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 2601.06973 — Baldelli et al., v3\n- 001 (pp1–3): Private State Interactive Tasks; public-history-only agents cannot retain privately chosen unresolved state. The theorem's assumptions exclude an externally supplied secret kept in a private prompt.\n- 002 (pp4–6): proof by indistinguishable public histories; fork-and-reveal test; Hangman and DDXPlus diagnosis; private CoT upper bound and explicit memory workflow variants.\n- 003 (pp7–9): 50 episodes per model/method/task, fork turn 4, five candidate secrets; workflow memory strong, public-history baselines weak. Counts leakage, overconfirmation, state substitution and denial; private CoT costs ~10x tokens.\n- 004 (pp10–12): conclusions and references; code chandar-lab/Hangman; architectural consistency guarantee is distinct from semantic noninterference.\n- 005 (pp13–15): related work and memory representation goals/facts/active notes; generated private state differs from retrieval of public facts.\n- 006 (pp16–18): example private states explicitly store a selected secret; retrieval baselines summarize rules and observations but omit chosen secret.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
