{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"One important caveat emerged from the steering literature: a method can nearly eliminate disclosure while severely degrading general response quality. The handoff will therefore require leakage, coherence, and secret-retention measurements together. For data, I’m using published concept probes and narrative-instruction examples, plus WritingPrompts as a source of story premises. None provides ready-made labels for premature plot revelations; that adaptation is documented separately."}}
